ℹ️ Kumari Chowk is a three-story red-brick palace built in 1757 by King Jaya Prakash Malla. It is the residence of the Royal Kumari of Kathmandu -- a prepubescent girl selected from the Newar Shakya community who is worshipped as the living incarnation of the Hindu goddess Taleju (a form of Durga)....</description>
